# =============================================================================
# PARTICIPANT DATA — must never be committed
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# This repository is public. Anything committed here stays in the git history
# permanently, even if deleted in a later commit. Raw and derived participant
# data are excluded by folder and by extension.
# =============================================================================
dat_triglycerides_change/
data/
dat/

*.xlsx
*.xls
*.csv
*.tsv
*.sav
*.dta
*.rds
*.rda
*.RDS
*.Rda
/*.R

# =============================================================================
# R
# =============================================================================
.Rproj.user/
.Rhistory
.RData
.Ruserdata
.Renviron
.Rapp.history

# =============================================================================
# Quarto
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# IMPORTANT: the patterns below are anchored to the repository root with a
# leading slash. An unanchored pattern such as `*_files/` would also match
# docs/<page>_files/, which holds the rendered figures — GitHub Pages would then
# serve the site with every image missing.
# =============================================================================
/.quarto/
/_freeze/
**/*.quarto_ipynb

# Render intermediates at the project root only
/*_cache/
/*_files/

# =============================================================================
# Rendered site — DO NOT IGNORE
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# GitHub Pages serves from docs/, so the whole folder must be committed,
# including docs/.nojekyll (which stops Jekyll from stripping files and folders
# whose names begin with an underscore). Quarto writes .nojekyll automatically;
# confirm it is present and tracked with:  git check-ignore -v docs/.nojekyll
# =============================================================================
# (nothing to ignore here — listed for clarity)

# =============================================================================
# Manuscript working files
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Uncomment if for_paper_codiet3/ holds drafts, figures or correspondence you
# would rather not publish. Leave commented if it is part of the public record.
# =============================================================================
# for_paper_codiet3/

# Word/LaTeX lock and temp files
~$*.docx
~$*.xlsx
*.log
*.aux
*.synctex.gz

# =============================================================================
# Operating system and editors
# =============================================================================
.DS_Store
.DS_Store?
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
desktop.ini
.vscode/
*.swp
*~

# =============================================================================
# Stray outputs written to the project root by scripts
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ggsave() in the diagnostic scripts writes PNGs to the working directory.
# Figures belong in the rendered site, not tracked separately.
# =============================================================================
/cmdi_tg_*.png
/*.pdf
